# Root .dockerignore for the monorepo build context used by all
# `services/*` and `apps/api`/`apps/web` Dockerfiles that bake from `.`.
#
# C36 (AUDIT.md): the build context previously shipped `node_modules`,
# `.git`, Dockerfiles themselves, *.md, tests, and editor cruft into every
# image build. That made `docker compose build` slow, bloated the image
# cache layers, and risked leaking the `*.md` design notes / `AUDIT.md` /
# `prompt.md` into published images. Excluding them keeps the context lean
# and the published image free of in-tree design notes.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Dependency manifests that are re-installed inside the image
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build outputs & caches
.next
dist
.turbo
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
.nyc_output

# Editor / OS cruft
.vscode
.idea
.cursor
.DS_Store

# Documentation & markdown (do NOT bake design notes / audit content
# into published images — they describe the repo, not the runtime).
docs
docs-site/docs
**/*.md
LICENSE
directorytree.md
AUDIT.md
prompt.md
todo.md

# Tests & test fixtures (the unit/integration suites are CI-only)
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/vitest.config.ts
**/jest.config.js

# Dockerfiles themselves and compose configs (the build context should not
# recursively include every compose file / Dockerfile of every service).
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
services/**/Dockerfile

# Local env files & secrets — never bake into the image
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.backup
*.bak

# Logs & runtime artifacts
*.log
api.err
api.log
**/*.log

# Misc APM / tooling artifacts not needed at runtime
.husky
.github
.turbo
